# Week 4: Exploratory Data Analysis and Feature Engineering

Week 4 is a **planning and design report**. It describes how the cleaned
public product, ingredient and review data will be explored and which
features will be built. It does **not** contain real-data results: the
Week 3 pipeline has been tested only on simulated rows, and the real
Sephora and Open Beauty Facts files have not yet been processed. Public
data have no verified `routine_dropout` label (that label is planned
from the future survey and routine diary), BRFS is my own proposed
framework without validated weights, and the five Week 1 hypotheses (H1
to H5) are still untested.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Item                                File
  ----------------------------------- ------------------------------------------------------
  Week 4 report (Word)                `reports/Week_4_EDA_Feature_Engineering_Report.docx`

  EDA workflow flowchart              `reports/figures/eda_workflow_flowchart.png`

  Feature engineering table (23       `docs/feature_engineering_table_week4.csv`
  proposed features, with status)     
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Feature status values: **Computable after real run (public data)**,
**Conditional (needs column or method check)**, **Future only (needs
survey / diary)**.

**Licensing note:** The licence terms of the source datasets must be
checked before data are downloaded, shared or committed. The Kaggle
licence of the Sephora dataset has not been verified. Open Beauty Facts
and INCIDB state ODbL terms (attribution and share-alike) on their own
pages; see Section 2.4 of the report.
